{%- comment -%}
  LBASS — HOMEPAGE ABOVE-THE-FOLD DENSITY (2026-08-10)
  Homepage only. Rendered from snippets/lbass-cro-tracking.liquid.

  ═══ WHAT THE PROBLEM ACTUALLY WAS ═══
  Measured on the live homepage at 901×1034:
      hero bottom ................ 1177px  (100svh)
      first product CARD ......... 2786px
      scroll needed to see it .... 1752px  ≈ 1.7 viewports

  The brief assumed padding. It wasn't. Between the hero and THE DROP sat five
  full sections totalling 1389px:
      .mq marquee ........  63px
      .lb-answer ......... 173px
      .trust-strip ....... 138px
      .intent-moments .... 277px
      .sec.inspect ....... 666px   ← the real blocker
  Section padding is only ~57px each, so zeroing ALL of it recovers ~250px of
  1752. Trimming padding alone could not have solved this. The lever is ORDER.

  ═══ WHY CSS ORDER AND NOT MOVING MARKUP ═══
  All 13 sections are direct children of <main>. templates/index.liquid is
  236KB and has already been the source of one storefront outage; cutting and
  re-pasting a section inside it is exactly the risky operation to avoid.
  Flex `order` achieves the same visual result, is reversible by deleting this
  file, and touches no markup.

  DOM order is preserved for SEO and for screen readers that follow source
  order — only the visual order changes. The .lb-answer AEO block still sits
  early in the HTML where answer engines read it; it simply renders below the
  products now.

  ═══ THE ORDER ═══
  hero → marquee → THE DROP (products) → answer → trust → intent → inspect →
  everything else in its original sequence.

  `main > *{order:10}` is required: flex items default to order:0, so without
  it every un-numbered section would jump ABOVE the numbered ones. Equal-order
  items keep DOM order, so the remaining seven sections stay in sequence.

  ═══ FLEX CAVEAT ═══
  Making <main> a flex column disables margin collapsing between sections.
  Verified after the change that this did not introduce extra vertical gaps —
  these sections use padding, not margin, for rhythm.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
/* ── 1. hero: 100svh → 82svh desktop, 76svh mobile ───────────────────────
   Keeps the badge, animated H1, both CTAs and the chips above the fold —
   verified — while returning ~190px to the page. */
.lbh{min-height:82svh!important}
@supports not (min-height:82svh){ .lbh{min-height:82vh!important} }
@media(max-width:767px){
  .lbh{min-height:76svh!important}
  @supports not (min-height:76svh){ .lbh{min-height:76vh!important} }
}

/* ── 2. visual reorder: products immediately after the marquee ────────── */
main{display:flex;flex-direction:column}
main > *{order:10}
main > .lbh,
main > #top,
main > .lbhs,
main > .lbcat{order:0}         /* hero carousel + Shop by category strip (2026-09-26); DOM order keeps the strip under the hero */
main > .mq{order:1}
main > #drop{order:2}          /* THE DROP — products */
main > .lb-answer{order:3}
main > .trust-strip{order:4}
main > .intent-moments{order:5}
main > #inspection{order:6}

/* ── 2b. products-first (2026-09-25) ──────────────────────────────────────
   The category nav and the full grid still sat below the storytelling, so
   the 65-product grid only began at screen 5.8 on mobile (375×812) and 4.5
   on desktop (1024×768). Measured after this block: 3.5 and 3.3.

   .lbhc is ALREADY the horizontal category nav — sneakers, Nike, Adidas,
   jackets, tees, pants, track pants, accessories, 1/1, full drop — with live
   counts. It only needed to move; no new nav was added. #cats further down
   duplicates its types and is a candidate to retire separately.

   These override the four order values set directly above by coming later
   at equal specificity. Nothing is hidden or deleted; delete this block to
   revert, exactly like the one above. */
main > .lbhc{order:5}          /* category nav */
main > #shop{order:6}          /* THE FULL GRID — 65 products */
main > .lbfr{order:10}         /* 2026-09-30 clothing-first homepage (strategic assessment): the fragrance
                                  best-sellers row sits right after «لوك كامل» (#shoplook, pinned to 9 below),
                                  i.e. after the full clothing grid, size shortcuts, intent and inspection.
                                  Was order:3 (directly under THE DROP). */
main > #shoplook{order:9}      /* same visual slot as before (first after #inspection); lets .lbfr follow it */
main > .lbbe{order:3}          /* K-beauty discovery (2026-09-26 night) — same slot, after .lbfr in DOM order */
main > .sec.shop-by{order:7}   /* size shortcuts S/M/L/XL + 41–44 */
main > .intent-moments{order:8}
main > #inspection{order:9}


/* The homepage already has one full trust reminder and one brand story.
   Suppress the repeated second/third versions so mobile visitors reach
   discovery, proof and the footer without another copy of the same pitch. */
main > .story-secondary,
main > .value-reminder.alt,
main > .value-reminder.dark{display:none!important}

/* ── 3. tighten the seam, not the whole page ──────────────────────────────
   Only the two edges that meet above the fold are trimmed (~35%). Sections
   further down keep their original rhythm so the page does not read as
   cramped once the customer is scrolling. */
main > .mq{padding-block:11px!important}
main > #drop{padding-top:38px!important}
@media(max-width:767px){
  main > #drop{padding-top:28px!important}
}
</style>
